$DATUM Synthesis of Compound 6. HB(C6F5)2 (96 mg, 0.277 mmol) and
dimesitylnorbornenylphosphane (100 mg, 0.276 mmol) were min. at r.t. to
give a yellow solution. Then a solution of benzaldehyde (40.0 mg, 0.377
mmol) in n-pentane (2.0 mL) was added to the solution of the FLP 4 and
instantaneous formation of a colorless precipitate was observed. The
reaction mixture was stirred at r.t. for 15 min. The volatiles were
removed under vacuum. The obtained residue was washed with n-pentane (3
mL) and dried under vacuum overnight. Compound 6 as a colorless solid
(166 mg, 85% yield). There is about 5% of an unidentified compound
present which could not be separated even by crystallization. Crystals of
compound 6 suitable for X-ray crystal structure analysis were obtained by
slow diffusion of n-pentane to a solution of compound 6 in CH2Cl2 at -35
°C. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CD2Cl2, 299 K): δ = 7.05 (br m, 1H, m-MesA), 7.04
(m, 1H, p-Ph), 7.00 (m, 2H, o-Ph), 6.99 (s, 1H, m-MesB), 6.92 (m, 2H,
m-Ph), 6.84 (br s, 1H, m′-MesA), 6.46 (d, 2 J PH = 13.5 Hz, CHO), 6.20
(br s, 1H, m′-MesB), 3.63 (m, 1H, PCH), 2.90 (s, 3H, o-CH3 Mes B), 2.88
(s, 3H, o-CH3 Mes A), 2.80 (br s, 1H, H-1), 2.43 (br s, 1H, H-4), 2.30
(s, 3H, p-CH3 Mes A), 2.18 (s, 3H, p-CH3 Mes B), 1.91 (s, 3H, o′-CH3 Mes
AMesA), 1.64 (dd, 3 J PH = 23.9 Hz, 3 J HH = 11.9 Hz, BCH), 1.39/1.01
(each m, each 1H, H-5), 1.13/0.78 (each m, each 1H, H-7), 0.95 (s, 3H,
o′-CH3 Mes B), 1.09/0.75 (each m, each 1H, H-6). 13C{1H} NMR (126 MHz,
CD2Cl2, 299 K): δ = 144.6 (d, 2 J PC = 4.4 Hz, o′-MesA), 143.8 (d, 4 J PC
= 3.0 Hz, p-MesA), 143.0 (d, 4 J PC = 3.2 Hz, p-MesB), 142.5 (d, 2 J PC =
7.5 Hz, o-MesB), 142.0 (d, 2 J PC = 11.7 Hz, o-MesA), 141.9 (d, 2 J PC =
8.6 Hz, o′-MesB-MesB), 138.5 (d, 3 J PC = 3.3 Hz, i-Ph), 132.7 (d, 3 J PC
= 11.8 Hz, m-MesA), 132.4 (d, 3 J PC = 10.7 Hz, m-MesB), 132.0 (d, 3 J PC
= 8.4 Hz, m′-MesA), 131.4 (d, 3 J PC = 10.1 Hz, m′-MesB), 128.4 (br d, 3
J PC = 5.9 Hz, o-Ph), 128.3 (d, 5 J PC = 3.3 Hz, p-Ph), 127.2 (d, 4 J PC
= 1.8 Hz, m-Ph), 121.6 (d, 1 J PC = 45.1 Hz, i-MesA), 120.9 (d, 1 J PC =
53.4 Hz, i-MesB), 87.6 (d, 1 J PC = 22.6 Hz, CHO), 42.5 (d, 2 J PC = 6.2
Hz, C-1), 41.6 (d, 3 J PC = 16.8 Hz, C-7), 40.3 (d, 1 J PC = 36.6 Hz,
PCH), 38.8 (br d, 3 J PC = 7.4 Hz, C-4), 35.1 (br, BCH), 34.1 (C-5), 27.0
(o-CH3 Mes A), 25.1 (d, 3 J PC = 5.6 Hz, o′-CH3 Mes B), 24.2 (d, 3 J PC =
4.9 Hz, o′-CH3 Mes A), 24.0 (br, o-CH3 Mes B), 22.4 (C-6), 21.1 (d, 5 J
PC = 1.4 Hz, p-CH3 Mes A), 20.8 (d, 5 J PC = 1.3 Hz, p-CH3 Mes B). [C6F5
not listed]. 11B{1H} NMR (160 MHz, CD2Cl2, 299 K): δ = 0.2 (ν 1/2 ≈ 150
Hz). 31P{1H} NMR (202 MHz, CD2Cl2, 299 K): δ = 38.9 (ν 1/2 ≈ 5 Hz). 19F
NMR (470 MHz, CD2Cl2, 213 K): δ = -130.2, -133.5, -134.2, -134.8 (each m,
1F each, o-C6F5), -160.5 (t, 3 J FF = 20.7 Hz, 1F, p-C6F5), -160.8 (t, 3
J FF = 21.6 Hz, 1F, p-C6F5), -164.3 (m, 1F, (m, 1F, m-C6F5), -165.1, (m,
2F, m-C6F5), -165.8, (m, 1F, m-C6F5). IR (KBr): ν/cm-1 = 2953 (vs), 2875
(s), 2361 (w), 2339 (w), 1640 (m), 1606 (m), 1512 (s), 1456 (vs).
Elemental analysis: calc. for C44H38PBF10O: C, 64.88; H, 4.70. Found: C,
63.20; H, 4.50. X-ray crystal structure analysis of compound 6: formula
C44H38BF10OP, M = 814.52, colorless crystal, 0.37 × 0.20 × 0.10 mm, a =
11.3261(2), b = 11.4019(2), c = 18.0739(4) Å, α = 80.106(4), β =
86.398(7), γ = 67.178(8)°, V = 2119.31(7) Å3, ρ calc = 1.276 g cm-3, μ =
0.141 mm-1, empirical absorption correction (0.949 ≤ T ≤ 0.986), Z = 2,
triclinic, space group P -1(No. 2), λ = 1.54178 Å, T = 223(2) K, ω and φ
scans, 16980 reflections collected ((±h, ± k, ± l)), [(sinθ)/λ] = 0.59
Å-1, 7239 independent (R int = 0.037) and 6197 observed reflections [I >
2σ(I)], 520 refined parameters, R = 0.067, wR2 = 0.199, max. (min.)
residual electron density 0.35 (-0.30) e Å-3, hydrogen atoms were
calculated and refined as riding atoms Melting point (DSC): 167 °C. 1H,
1H GCOSY (500 MHz, CD2Cl2, 299 K): δ 1H / 1H = 7.04 / 6.92 (p-Ph / m-Ph),
7.05 / 6.85, 2.88, 2.30, 1.91 (m-MesA / m´-MesA, o-CH3 Mes A, p-CH3 Mes
A, o´-CH3 Mes A), 7.00 / 6.92 (o-Ph / m-Ph), 6.99 / 6.20, 2.90, 2.18,
0.95 (m-MesB / m´-MesB, o-CH3 Mes B, p-CH3 Mes B, o´-CH3 Mes B), 6.46 /
2.88, 0.95 (CHO / o-CH3 Mes A, o´-CH3 Mes B), 6.20 / 6.99, 2.90, 2.18,
0.95 (m´-MesB / m-MesB, o-CH3 Mes B, p-CH3 Mes B, o´-CH3 Mes B), 3.63 /
2.80, 1.64, 1.09 (H-2 / H-1, H-3, H-6), 2.90 / 6.99, 6.20, 2.18, 0.95
(o-CH3 Mes B / m-MesB, m´-MesB, p-CH3 Mes B, o´-CH3 Mes B), 2.88 / 7.05,
6.85, 2.30, 1.91 (o-CH3 Mes A / m-MesA, m´-MesA, p-CH3 Mes A, o´-CH3 Mes
A), 2.80 / 3.63, 2.43, 1.13, 0.78 (H-1 / H-2, H-4, H-7), 2.43 / 2.80,
1.64, 1.39, 1.13, 0.78 (H-4 / H-1, H-3, H-5, H-7), 2.30 / 7.05, 6.85,
