$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Bis-borylation of Terminal Dialkynes: Complex 1
(0.0025 mmol, 0.2 mol%) was placed in a vial and cold pinacolborane (3
mmol) and toluene (3 ml) were added. The resulting suspension was stirred
for five minutes at room temperature to get a clear yellow solution,
which was again cooled (ca. -15 °C). To this solution, cold terminal
dialkyne (1.25 mmol) was added dropwise under stirring and the reaction
mixture was allowed to stir at room temperature. Progress of the reaction
was monitored by GC analysis and the products were isolated by column
chromatography over silica gel using ethylacetate/hexane mixture as
eluent.
1,4-Bis((Z)-2-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)ethenyl)benzene3,
white solid, yield 85%. Mp 7.10 (d, J = 14.9 Hz, 2H), 5.50 (d, J = 14.9
Hz, 2H), 1.22 (s, 24H). 13C-NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ 147.80 (CH), 138.13
(quat-C), 128.39 (CH), 83.51(OC), 24.83 (CH3). MS (ESI) m/z 382.4 (M+,
8%), 279.3 (26%), 167.2 (37%), 149.2 (100%), 129.2 (22%), 86 (56%).
HR/MS: calcd (C22H32O4B2)+ 382.2481. Found: 382.2484
