$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Cu-Catalyzed α-Borylation of Thioacetylenes. To a
mixture of CuCl (5.0 mg, 0.05 mmol), Xantphos (28.8 mg, 0.05 mmol), and
NaOt-Bu (9.6 mg, 0.1 mmol) in 0.5 mL of toluene was added neat HBpin (150
μL, 1.0 mmol) under a nitrogen atmosphere. After stirring at 0 °C for 15
min, 1a (0.5 mmol) was added at 0 °C, followed by stirring at 25 °C for
12 h (determined by GC). The reaction mixture was concentrated and
purified by column chromatography (petroleum ether/EtOAc = 20:1) on
silica gel to give 4a. Colorless oil, yield 120 mg (83%). Rf = 0.35
(petroleum ether/EtOAc = 20:1); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ 1.22 (t, J =
7.4 Hz, 3H), 1.34 (s, 12H), 2.95 (q, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 7.23-7.28 (m, 1H),
7.30 (s, 1H), 7.33-7.38 (m, 2H), 7.64 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ 15.4, 24.7, 27.6, 84.1, 127.7, 127.9, 130.1, 137.0,
141.0; MS (EI, m/z): 290 (M+, 100), 275 (3), 229 (1), 163 (4); HRMS (EI)
calcd for C16H23BO2S (M+) 290.1512, found 290.1507.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, optimization study (optimized on
ligands, copper sources and solvents)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of (Z)-1-Thio- and (Z)-2-Thio-1-alkenyl Boronates via
Copper-Catalyzed Regiodivergent Hydroboration of Thioacetylenes: An
Experimental and Theoretical Study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
