$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Bis-borylation of
Terminal Dialkynes: Complex 1 (0.0025 mmol, 0.2 mol%) was placed in a
vial and cold pinacolborane (3 mmol) and toluene (3 ml) were added. The
resulting suspension was stirred for five minutes at room temperature to
get a clear yellow solution, which was again cooled (ca. -15 °C). To this
solution, cold terminal dialkyne (1.25 mmol) was added dropwise under
stirring and the reaction mixture was allowed to stir at room
temperature. Progress of the reaction was monitored by GC analysis and
the products were isolated by column chromatography over silica gel using
ethylacetate/hexane mixture as eluent.
1,3-Bis((Z)-2-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)vinyl)propane,
colorless oil, yield 82%. IR (neat): 2980, 2928, 2859, 1626, 1425, 1369,
1321, 1142, 969, 876, 841, 756 cm-1. 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 6.39 (dt,
J = 13.8, 7.1 Hz, 2H), 5.26 (d, J = 13.5 Hz, 2H), 2.38-2.32 (m, 4H), 1.41
(quintet, J = 7.4 Hz, 2H), 1.19 (s, 24H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ
154.90 (CH), 82.76 (OC), 31.69 (CH2), 29.52 (CH2), 24.86 (CH3). MS (ESI)
m/z 348.4 (M+, 2%), 291.3 (6%), 279.3 (12%), 248.3 (13%), 220.3 (12%),
167.2 (17%), 149.2 (47%), 121.2 (9%), 101.3 (30%), 82.4 (100%). HR/MS:
calcd (C19H34O4B2)+ 348.2638. Found: 348.2650
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
