$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4. Asymmetric Rhodium-Directed
anti-Markovnikov Regioselective Boracyclopentannulation General
Procedure: A 10 mL oven-dried Schlenk flask was charged with the
appropriate NHC-BH3 (0.125 mmol), [Rh(nbd)2]BF4 (2.5 mg, 6.2 μmol, 5
mol%) and (S)-Xylyl-MeO-BIPHEP (3.6 mg, 6.2 μmol, 5 mol%) under argon.
Then, dry degassed dichloromethane (1 mL) was added and the mixture was
stirred at room temperature under argon for 2 minutes. The crude product
was filtered through a short plug of silica gel using dichloromethane (10
mL) as eluent to give the desired cyclic NHC-borane. The title compound
was filtered through a short plug of silica gel using dichloromethane (10
mL) as eluent to give 2e in 80% yield as colorless oil. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ (ppm) 0.90-1.75 (m, 2H), 1.11 (bs, 3H), 1.95 (bs, 1H), 3.47 (dd,
1H, 2J = 10.8 Hz, 3J = 5.3 Hz), 3.66 (s, 3H), 4.07 (dd, 1H, 2J = 10.8 Hz,
3J = 8.5 Hz), 6.79 (d, 1H, 3J = 1.7 Hz), 6.81 (d, 1H, 3J = 1.7 Hz). 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) 21.9, 26.8(HMQC), 35.8, 58.9, 116.3, 122.6.
11B NMR (128 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm) -23.6 (t, 1JB-H = 88.7 Hz). HRMS (ES,
[M+Na]+) calcd for [C7H13BN2Na]+: 159.1063; found: 159.1060 FT-IR (ATR) ν
(cm-1) 3360 (w), 3131 (w), 2943 m), 2854 (w), 2284 (s), 1676 (w), 1566
(w), 1494 (w), 1454 (w), 1411 (w), 1368 (w), 1337 (w), 1273 (w), 1196
(w), 1165 (w), 1065 (w), 998 (w), 960 (w), 803 (w), 721 (w), 619 (w).
HPLC: Enantiomeric excess was determined by HPLC with a Chiralcel OD-3,
Hexane/isopropanol 80/20 1 mL/min, UV 220 nm et CD 220nm; rt (major) =
7.1 min, rt (minor)= 8.8 min; 95.8:4.2 er.[α]20 D: +1.1, c = 1, CHCl3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, anti-Morkovnikov reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Rhodium-Directed anti-Markovnikov Regioselective
Boracyclopentannulation
