$DATUM 1634-04-4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Catalytic Olefin
Hydroboration. In a typical experiment, a scintillation vial (with a
magnetic stir bar) was charged in the glovebox with 0.64 mL tertbutyl
methyl ether, 0.64 mmol (1 eq) of the desired olefin, 0.67 mmol (1.05 eq)
of pinacolborane, 0.64 mmol (1 eq) cyclooctane internal standard, and 1
mol% of the cobalt pre-catalyst. The vial was capped and the mixture was
stirred at 23 ºC until the reaction was complete. The reaction was
monitored by analysis of aliquots by gas chromatography. Upon completion,
the mixture was concentrated, diluted with hexane and passed through a
silica plug in a Pasteur pipette and concentrated in vacuo. The resulting
solution was concentrated and then analyzed by GC-FID, 1H NMR, and 13C
NMR to determine the purity, identity, and regioisomeric and
diastereomeric ratio of products. Partial conversions were determined by
comparing the ratio of substrate to internal standard to the ratio
obtained in an initial aliquot taken at the beginning of the reaction.
2-octyl-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane (A-i).
2-(2,3,3-trimethylbutyl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane (I). The
title compound was isolated as a colorless oil. 1H NMR (500 MHz,
chloroform-d, 23 ºC) δ 1.53 (app ddt, J HH = 10.8, 6.9, 3.5 Hz, 1H,
tBuCHCH3), 1.26 (s, 6H, two of pinacol CH3), 1.25 (s, 6H, two of pinacol
CH3), 0.95 (dd, J HH = 15.4, 3.7 Hz, 1H, one of CH2BPin), 0.86 (d, J HH =
6.4 Hz, 3H, tBuCHCH3), 0.83 (s, 9H, tBu methyls), 0.50 (dd, J HH = 15.2,
11.1 Hz, 1H, one of CH2BPin). 13C NMR (126 MHz, chloroform-d, 23 ºC): δ
83.0 (CH0, pinacol C(CH3)2), 39.2 (CH3), 33.5 (CH0, tBu C(CH3)3), 27.2
(CH3), 25.1 (CH3), 24.8 (CH3), 17.5 (CH3) ppm. GCMS m/z (% relative
intensity, ion) 226.2 (0.03%, M+), 211.2 (6%, M+-15), 171.1 (12%, M+-55),
126.2 (6%, M+-100), 101.1 (17%, M+-125), 83.1 (18%, M+-143), 69.1 (14%,
M+-157), 57.1 (26%, M+-169).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed scintillation vial used, optimization study, optimized on catalyst
and time, glovebox used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
