$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-(3-Methoxyphenyl)propanoic acid ethyl ester
9a. N,N,N',N'-tetramethylethylenediamine (TMEDA) (7 μL, 0.05 mmol) was
added to a stirred solution of FeCl2·4H2O (10 mg, 0.05 mmol) in anhydrous
THF (5 mL) under nitrogen and stirred for 5 mins. 0.5 mL of this solution
was transferred to a flask containing 6.5 mL anhydrous tetrahydrofuran
under nitrogen. 3-Methoxystyrene (0.14 mL, 1.0 mmol) was added to the
flask and ethylmagnesium bromide (3 M in Et2O, 0.50 mL, 1.5 mmol) was
added dropwise. The reaction was stirred for 2 h and the electrophile
(1.6 mmol) added, either neat or as a solution in anhydrous THF (1 M), at
room temperature or at-78 °C. The reaction was stirred for a further 2 h
and quenched with aqueous sulphate buffer solution or water (10 mL). The
phases were separated and the aqueous phase extracted with Et2O (3 × 10
mL). The combined organic extracts were washed with water (10 mL) and
brine (10 mL), dried (MgSO4) and the solvent removed in vacuo. The
product was purified by flash silica chromatography.
2-(1-(3-Methoxyphenyl)ethyl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane 9o.
General procedure B was applied to 3-methoxystyrene (0.14 mL, 1.0 mmol),
FeCl2·4H2O (1.0 mg, 0.005 mmol), TMEDA (0.7 μL, 0.005 mmol),
ethylmagnesium bromide (3 M in Et2O, 0.50 mL, 1.5 mmol) and pinacol
borane (0.23 mL, 1.6 mmol). The crude product was purified by flash
chromatography (pet. ether/Et2O/NEt 3 97:2:1→93:6:1) to give 9o as a
colourless oil (129 mg, 45%). Rf 0.52 (9:1 pet. ether/Et2O); 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.19 (1H, t, J = 8.0 Hz, ArH), 6.84-6.81 (1H, m, ArH),
6.81-6.78 (1H, m, ArH), 6.70 (1H, ddd, J = 8.0, 2.5, 1.0 Hz, ArH), 3.80
(3H, s, OCH3), 2.42 (1H, q, J = 7.5 Hz, CHCH3), 1.33 (3H, d, J = 7.5 Hz,
CHCH3), 1.23 (6H, s, C(CH3)a(CH3)bC(CH3)a(CH3)b), 1.22 (6H, s,
C(CH3)a(CH3)bC(CH3)a(CH3)b); 13C NMR (125.8 MHz, CDCl3) δ (CH resonance
not resolved) 159.6 (C), 146.6 (C), 129.1 (CH), 120.3 (CH), 113.5 (CH),
110.5 (CH), 83.3 (2 × C), 55.1 (CH3), 24.6 (2 × CH3), 24.6 (2 × CH3),
17.0 (CH3); 11 B (128 MHz, CDCl3) δ33.6.
