$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 110-71-4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-2-[(1R)-1-phenylethyl]-1,3,2-dioxaborolane [(R)-11]
The following procedure was taken from the Crudden modification16 of the
Hayashi method17 for the rhodium-catalyzed asymmetric hydroboration of
styrene. Two 25 mL roundbottom flasks were equipped with stir bars,
flame-dried under high vacuum, cooled and filled with argon. DME (12 mL)
was added to one flask and the flask was degassed by two freezepump-thaw
cycles. [Rh(COD)2]+BF4 -(123.8 mg, 0.305 mmol, 5 mol%)18 and
(R)-(+)-BINAP (143.0 mg, 0.335 mmol, 5.5 mol%) and DME (8 mL) were added
to the second flask, and the mixture was stirred for ten minutes at room
temperature. Styrene (R) (699 μL, 6.10 mmol) was added and the solution
was cooled to -78 °C. Freshly distilled catecholborane (S) (711 μL, 6.71
mmol) was dissolved in the remaining DME and added via syringe to the
reaction over 30 minutes. The reaction mixture was stirred at -78 °C for
four hours. Pinacol (U) (1514 mg, 12.81 mmol) was added at -78 °C and the
reaction mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature with stirring
overnight. High vacuum (0.5 mm Hg) was used to concentrate the reaction
mixture. The crude black oil was purified by column chromatography
(silica gel, 50 mL of hexanes and 200 mL of 5% EtOAc/hexanes). (R)-11
(1.109 g, 78%) as a colorless oil. Regioselectivity of the reaction was
judged to be 70:1 by NMR (q, 2.43: t, 2.75 ppm). Enantiomeric excess was
found to be 88% by GC analysis of the corresponding alcohols obtained
from peroxide oxidation as described below. The enantiomeric excess (88%
ee) obtained in the catalytic enantioselective hydroboration procedure
was determined by oxidation of (R)-11 to (R)-1-phenylethanol and chiral
GC analysis using a β-cyclodextrin column.16 IR (thin film): 3017, 2977,
2874, 1493, 1454, 1377, 1355, 1322, 1262, 1213, 1144, 844, 700 cm-1. 1H
NMR: δ 7.28-7.12 (m, 5H), 2.43 (q, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 1.33 (d, J = 7.4 Hz,
3H), 1.20 (d, J = 3.4 Hz, 12H); 13C NMR: δ 145.0, 128.3, 127.8, 125.0,
119.7, 83.3, 24.6, 17.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
