$DATUM [C5H5B(CH2)3OCH2CH=CH2]2YCl (5). A toluene solution of allyl ether (256
mg, 2.61 mmol in 1 mL of toluene) was added to 1 (73 mg, 0.262 mmol) in 2
mL of toluene. After stirring for 37 h at room temperature, the reaction
mixture was filtered. Evaporation of the filtrate in vacuo left an orange
oil, which was washed with 4 × 0.5 mL of cold hexane and dried in vacuo.
5 as an orange oil (95 mg, 77% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, C6D6, 25 °C): δ
7.48 (bs, 4H, 3-/5-H), 6.72 (bd, J H-H = 10.0 Hz, 4H, 2-/6-H), 6.29 (tt,
J H-H = 7.2 Hz, J H-H = 1.6 Hz, 2H, 4-H), 5.82-5.72 (m, 2H, OCH2CHCH2),
5.11 (dd, 2H, J H-H = 17.2 Hz, J H-H = 1.6 Hz, OCH2CHCHH'), 5.01 (d, 2H,
J H-H = 10.4 Hz, OCH2CHCHH'), 3.93 (bs, 4H, OCH 2CHCH2), 3.32(t, 4H, J
H-H = 5.6 Hz, BCH2CH2CH 2O), 1.81 (bs, 4H, BCH2CH 2CH2O), 1.44 (t, J H-H
= 7.6 Hz, 4H, BCH 2CH2CH2O). 13C NMR (100 MHz, C6D6, 25 °C): δ 141.6,
133.5, 130.6, 118.9, 111.8, 74.6, 73.8, 27.6, 18.6. 11B NMR (128 MHz,
C6D6, 25 °C): δ 41.8. 89Y NMR (19.6 MHz, C6D6, 25 °C): δ -15.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stoichiometry 1:10, anti-Markovnikov selective, product
depends on reaction stoichiometry and temp.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rapid entry to functionalized boratabenzene complexes through
metal-induced hydroboration at the anionic 1-H-boratabenzene ligand
